	(text "The cable from the controller\nis connected through an RJ-45\nconnector - a model which is low\nprofile with respect to the PCB.\nVCC is 8V, I2C sits at 3V3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "170299e7-23f6-41b0-83c0-d0f20432b35c")
	)
	(text "3dB 50Ohm pad"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.674 128.778 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "18a823de-ab68-474b-bea3-db3e1aa1e030")
	)
	(text "ADS1115 - 16-bit delta-sigma ADC, I2C address 0x48 (ADDR=GND)\nMeasures AD8307 OUT differentially against detector COM (AIN0-AIN1),\nPGA ±4.096 V, continuous mode 128 SPS, set by firmware on hot-plug.\nC_filt 100 nF with the AD8307's 12.5 kΩ output impedance: ~130 Hz video filter.\nAIN1 routed to AD8307 COM pin, not to a nearby GND via.\nALERT/RDY unused, pulled up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 142.748 32.766 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "38faf0e4-119d-4675-a94e-edd8580474c0")
	)
	(text "MCP9808 digital temperature sensor, ±0.25 °C typ, 0.0625 °C resolution,\nI2C address 0x18 (A0, A1, A2 = GND). VDD from +3V3 with 100n at the pin.\nPurpose: track the detector die temperature, not ambient. Log detectors\ndrift roughly ±0.3 dB over -40 to +85 °C; the firmware reads this sensor\n(MEAS:TEMP?) so each head's drift can be characterised and compensated.\nPlace as close to the AD8307 as possible, same side of the board, on the\nsame ground pour, with no slot or thermal relief between them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.448 27.432 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5b0cf9fb-45a9-4212-a603-a6c0486da4be")
	)
	(text "The VCC on the cable from\nthe controller is at 8V or\nthereabouts, for the AD8307\nit is best to control down to \n3V3, since the I2C from the\ncontroller sits at 3V3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.728 28.448 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "87126f1c-3bd5-4f0f-9d6a-006526263628")
	)
	(text "AD8307 logarithmic detector, 500 MHz, 25 mV/dB, intercept -84 dBm at INP.\nRF path: SMA -> 3 dB pi pad (17.4R series, 2x 294R shunt) -> 52.3R termination\n-> C1 10n C0G -> INP. The pad gives the SMA a stable 50R match regardless of\nthe detector's ~1.1k || 1.4p input and raises max input to +20 dBm; the pad\nplus termination together shift the intercept to -81 dBm at the SMA.\nINM is AC-grounded through C2 10n, identical to C1, so both inputs see the\nsame impedance and ground noise cancels. Do not DC-ground INP or INM.\nR4 and C2 return to one via field at pins 1/2; nothing else uses it.\nOUT (12.5k internal) drives ADS1115 AIN0 directly;\nintercept and slope corrections live in the head EEPROM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.368 97.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8f21176d-d328-4c7e-a5ae-fc0c03a27a34")
	)
	(text "Extra pull up in the\nsensor head, and tvs\ndiodes for protection on \nthe I2C lines"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.196 116.078 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "db083faa-a973-4c46-8057-d0a11e4fbfb5")
	)
